# Greedy Freebooter: "When this creature DIES" (CR 700.4: put into a graveyard from the battlefield). Bot2 exiles it with
# Swords to Plowshares: it never reaches a graveyard, so there is no scry and no Treasure token (the positive control, a
# Freebooter that does die, is in the other scenarios). Bot1 gains the 1 life from Swords and is asked to scry nothing.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Greedy Freebooter
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains
Mountain
Island
Forest

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Swords to Plowshares
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Greedy Freebooter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Swords to Plowshares.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Greedy Freebooter)
[T2 Bot2.Main2]
! Bot1.Arrange

[Expect]
Exile = Greedy Freebooter
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Swamp
Bot1.Life = 21
Bot1.Library = Mountain; Island; Forest
